    "final_answer": "I successfully found and documented a popular chocolate chip cookie recipe from Allrecipes.com. Here are the complete details:\n\n## 🍪 Best Chocolate Chip Cookies\n**Source:** https://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/10813/best-chocolate-chip-cookies/\n**Popularity:** 19,463 ratings • **Yield:** 48 servings\n\n### Ingredients\n| Quantity | Ingredient |\n|----------|------------|\n| 1 cup | butter, softened |\n| 1 cup | white sugar |\n| 1 cup | packed brown sugar |\n| 2 | large eggs |\n| 2 teaspoons | vanilla extract |\n| 1 teaspoon | baking soda |\n| 2 teaspoons | hot water |\n| ½ teaspoon | salt |\n| 3 cups | all-purpose flour |\n| 2 cups | semisweet chocolate chips |\n| 1 cup | chopped walnuts (optional) |\n\n### Preparation Steps (Directions)\n1. **Gather your ingredients** — Make sure your butter is softened and your eggs are at room temperature.\n2. **Preheat the oven** to 350°F (175°C). Lightly grease the baking sheets.\n3. **Cream the butter and sugars** — Beat the butter, white sugar, and brown sugar with an electric mixer in a large bowl until smooth and creamy (1–2 minutes). Beat in the eggs and vanilla extract until combined. Dissolve the baking soda in the hot water; add to the batter along with the salt, and mix until combined.\n4. **Add the dry ingredients** — Stir in the flour, chocolate chips, and walnuts until a soft dough forms.\n5. **Portion the dough** — Drop rounded spoonfuls of cookie dough about 2 inches apart onto the ungreased baking sheets.\n6. **Bake** in the preheated oven until the edges are lightly browned, about **10 minutes**.\n7. **Cool** on the baking sheets briefly before transferring to a wire rack to cool completely. Store in an airtight container or serve immediately.\n\n### Notes\n- This is the highest-rated chocolate chip cookie recipe on Allrecipes.com with nearly 20,000 ratings.\n- A serving-size adjuster (½×, 1×, 2×) is available on the original page.\n- Walnuts are optional and can be omitted or substituted.",
